@knowledge adoc
@viewpoints specification
@description {
  Concepts and operations of adoc, a harness-independent framework in which an agent edits plugin-defined documents kept in git, a user reads the rendered documents in a web UI, and the user's comments and actions reach the agent as one-time messages, with plugin code optionally changing documents on the user's actions.
}
@scope {
  Cover the workspace, its home directory and configuration, the command line and MCP surfaces, plugins and the interface they implement, documents and their identifiers and versions, references between documents, rendering markup and actions, user messages with their format and delivery, the server and web UI, and the checks and warnings.
  Exclude concrete plugins such as TODO, TASK or KANBAN, the visual layout of the web UI, change history, authentication and real-time concurrent editing.
}

concept _Adoc_Workspace_ in workspace = {
  A directory that adoc manages, normally a git repository, holding one _Adoc_Home_.
.relations
  references _Document_Version_
  holds _Adoc_Home_
  contains _Document_
  git shown by _Adoc_Web_UI_
  git checked by _Adoc_Check_Command_
  served by _Adoc_Server_
.contract
  - Git must be the version control of every _Document_ in an _Adoc_Workspace_; adoc itself must not require git to run.
  - An _Adoc_Web_UI_ must show whether the _Adoc_Workspace_ is inside a git repository, and _Adoc_Check_Command_ must report a warning when it is not.
  - An _Adoc_Workspace_ must not keep change history apart from git commits.
.remarks
  - Chosen: git commit messages stand in for change history and comment threads.
  - Chosen: a missing git repository is shown, not refused, because adoc never calls git; a future git-related field, such as a commit hash, shows "no git" instead.
  - Non-goal: real-time concurrent editing. Conflicting writes are refused through _Document_Version_, not merged.
}

concept _Adoc_Home_ in workspace = {
  The `.adoc` directory of an _Adoc_Workspace_, which holds the _Adoc_Config_ and selects the workspace for every command.
.relations
  part of _Adoc_Workspace_
  holds _Adoc_Config_
  selected by _Adoc_CLI_
.contract
  - The _Adoc_CLI_ must select the _Adoc_Home_ from the `--home` option first, then the `ADOC_HOME` environment variable, then the nearest `.adoc` directory from the current directory upward.
  - The _Adoc_CLI_ must refuse a workspace command when no _Adoc_Home_ is found, and name the `adoc init` command.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the same discovery order as aterm.
}

concept _Adoc_Config_ in workspace = {
  The file `.adoc/adoc.yaml` that declares the plugins, the watch paths, the assigned agent with its message transport, the server address and the default colour scheme of the web UI of one _Adoc_Workspace_.
.relations
  references _adoc:Plugin_Directory_
  references _adoc:Agent_Claim_
  configures _Adoc_Workspace_
  inside _Adoc_Home_
  declares _Plugin_
  assigns _Plugin_Key_
  declares _Watch_Path_
  declares _Assigned_Agent_
  configures _User_Message_Transport_
  configures _Adoc_Server_
  configures _Web_UI_Theme_
.contract
  - Each _Plugin_ declared in an _Adoc_Config_ must name its source as a bare name looked up in the _Plugin_Directory_ entries, a local path or an npm package, and the _Plugin_Key_ under which it is used.
  - An _Adoc_Config_ must declare exactly one _Assigned_Agent_ with a name and one _User_Message_Transport_ with the settings of its kind.
  - An _Adoc_Config_ must declare the host and port of the _Adoc_Server_.
  - An _Adoc_Config_ may declare the default colour scheme of the _Web_UI_Theme_ as `ui.theme`: dark, light or system; dark when it is not declared.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the _Adoc_Config_ assigns the _Plugin_Key_, so one plugin package may serve two keys in one workspace.
  - Example: `plugins: [{key: TODO, from: ./.adoc/plugins/todo}]`, `watch: [docs]`, `agent: {name: adoc-dev, transport: {kind: herdr}}`, `server: {host: 0.0.0.0, port: 7700}`, `ui: {theme: dark}`.
  - Chosen: the herdr kind needs no target in the _Adoc_Config_; the target comes from the _Agent_Claim_.
}

concept _Watch_Path_ in workspace = {
  A directory declared in _Adoc_Config_ under which the _Adoc_Server_ watches files to find and track every _Document_.
.relations
  filtered by _Plugin_Key_
  inspected by _Adoc_Check_Command_
  declared in _Adoc_Config_
  watched by _Adoc_Server_
  holds _Document_
.contract
  - A _Document_ outside every _Watch_Path_ must not be visible to adoc.
  - A file under two overlapping _Watch_Path_ entries must count once.
  - A file under a _Watch_Path_ whose name does not start with a declared _Plugin_Key_ and a hyphen must be ignored, except as stated by _Adoc_Check_Command_.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the location of a _Document_ is not fixed. A directory per plugin under docs, such as `docs/tasks/`, is recommended.
}

concept _Assigned_Agent_ in workspace = {
  The single agent that receives every _User_Message_ of an _Adoc_Workspace_ and edits its documents, identified by the _Agent_Claim_ when it runs in a herdr pane.
.relations
  belongs to _Adoc_Workspace_
  identified by _Agent_Claim_
  receives _User_Message_
  edits _Document_
  reads _Plugin_Skill_
  commits changes of _Plugin_Action_Handler_
.contract
  - An _Adoc_Workspace_ must have exactly one _Assigned_Agent_.
  - An _Assigned_Agent_ must change a _Document_ by editing its files directly.
  - An _Assigned_Agent_ must read the current file of a _Document_ before editing it, because a _Plugin_Action_Handler_ may have changed it.
  - An _Assigned_Agent_ must commit its changes to git explicitly, together with any uncommitted change made by a _Plugin_Action_Handler_.
.remarks
  - Chosen: adoc provides no generic editing operation and no editing command for the agent.
  - Chosen: adoc never commits on its own.
  - Chosen: one agent for now. Several agents may be allowed later.
}

concept _Adoc_CLI_ in surface = {
  The `adoc` command line, whose commands take the form `adoc <noun> <verb>` in the manner of aterm and serve both people and the _Assigned_Agent_.
.relations
  references _adoc:Plugin_
  serves _Assigned_Agent_
  references _Document_
  selects _Adoc_Home_
  shared with _Adoc_MCP_Tool_
  includes _User_Message_Wait_Command_
  includes _Adoc_Check_Command_
  includes _Browser_Open_Command_
  includes _Agent_Claim_Command_
  includes _Document_Find_Command_
  includes _Skill_Install_Command_
  runs _Skill_Check_
  finds server by _Server_Record_
  starts _Adoc_Server_
  shows _Plugin_Skill_
.contract
  - The _Adoc_CLI_ must provide `adoc init`, `adoc server run`, `adoc mcp run`, `adoc message wait`, `adoc message list`, `adoc plugin list`, `adoc document list`, `adoc document search`, `adoc skill list`, `adoc skill view`, `adoc skill install`, `adoc skill update`, `adoc skill uninstall`, `adoc ui list`, `adoc ui open`, `adoc agent claim`, `adoc agent show` and `adoc check`.
  - Every command of the _Adoc_CLI_, also through the _Adoc_MCP_Tool_, must run the _Skill_Check_ and show what it finds as warnings.
  - Every finite result of the _Adoc_CLI_ must support `--output text`, `--output markdown`, `--output json` and `--output yaml`, with text as the default.
  - A command of the _Adoc_CLI_ that needs the running _Adoc_Server_ must find it through the _Server_Record_ and must fail with a clear error when no _Adoc_Server_ is running.
  - Every command of the _Adoc_CLI_ must answer `--help` with its usage, behavior and an example.
.remarks
  - Chosen: no command edits a _Document_; the agent edits files directly.
  - Chosen: `adoc skill` lists, shows and installs every _Agent_Skill_: `adoc` for the assigned agent's workflow, `adoc-plugin-authoring` for writing plugins, and the _Plugin_Skill_ of each _Plugin_.
  - Chosen: `bin/adoc` in the adoc repository runs the command line of that checkout.
}

concept _Adoc_MCP_Tool_ in surface = {
  The single MCP tool `adoc` with the arguments `cmd` and `stdin`, which runs any command of the _Adoc_CLI_ without the executable prefix, in the manner of aterm.
.relations
  mirrors _Adoc_CLI_
  served by _Adoc_Server_
  started by _Adoc_CLI_
.contract
  - The _Adoc_MCP_Tool_ must accept `cmd` as an _Adoc_CLI_ command line without the leading `adoc`, and `stdin` as the text that the command would read from standard input.
  - The _Adoc_MCP_Tool_ must return the same result as the same command of the _Adoc_CLI_.
  - `adoc mcp run` must serve the _Adoc_MCP_Tool_ over stdio, and with `--with-server` must also host the _Adoc_Server_ in the same process.
  - An _Adoc_Server_ must serve the _Adoc_MCP_Tool_ over HTTP at `/mcp`.
  - Over stdio, standard output must carry only MCP messages, and diagnostics must go to standard error.
  - The _Adoc_MCP_Tool_ must refuse process and installation commands, such as `server run`, `mcp run` and `skill install`.
.remarks
  - Example: `adoc({cmd: "message wait"})`.
}

concept _Plugin_ in plugin = {
  A package that defines one kind of _Document_ by implementing the _Plugin_Interface_, and that an _Adoc_Config_ binds to one _Plugin_Key_.
.relations
  bound by _Adoc_Config_
  implements _Plugin_Interface_
  identified by _Plugin_Key_
  defines _Document_
  provides _Plugin_Renderer_
  provides _Plugin_Action_Handler_
  provides _Plugin_Skill_
  returns _Document_Summary_
  decides form of _Document_Anchor_
  shown as _Plugin_Tab_
  permits _Document_Reference_
  loaded by _Adoc_Server_
.contract
  - A _Plugin_ must decide whether each of its documents is one file or one folder, and in which file format.
  - A _Plugin_ must decide the form of the _Document_Anchor_ values of its documents.
  - A _Plugin_ must not read or embed data of another _Plugin_; a _Document_Reference_ is the only connection allowed.
  - When a _Plugin_ fails to load, the _Adoc_Server_ must still start, and its _Plugin_Tab_ must show the load error.
.remarks
  - Example: a TODO plugin and a specification plugin may both store Markdown and still be different plugins.
}

concept _Plugin_Interface_ in plugin = {
  The object a _Plugin_ default-exports from its `index.ts` through `definePlugin` of the _Plugin_Kit_: description, layout, summarize, render, and the optional renderChanges and actions.
.relations
  references _adoc:Adoc_Web_UI_
  implemented by _Plugin_
  declared with _Plugin_Kit_
  called by _Adoc_Server_
  takes _Document_
  receives _Document_Key_
  summarize returns _Document_Summary_
  render runs _Plugin_Renderer_
  actions run _Plugin_Action_Handler_
  returns text of _User_Action_Message_
  feeds _Document_Summary_List_
  references _Document_Version_
.contract
  - Every function of the _Plugin_Interface_ that concerns one _Document_ must receive the _Document_Key_, its plugin key, its local id, its path, its main file, the text of the main file and the texts of all its files.
  - The layout must be either a file with an extension, such as `.md`, optionally with companion extensions such as `.png`, or a folder with an entry file name, such as `bug.yaml`.
  - Companion files must not be handed to the functions of the _Plugin_Interface_, since they may be binary.
  - The summarize function must return one _Document_Summary_; a thrown error is the parse error.
  - The render function must return the body HTML; a thrown error is the parse error.
  - The optional renderChanges function must receive the current _Document_ and an earlier version of it and return body HTML that shows the changes; without it, the _Adoc_Web_UI_ must show a line diff of the main file.
  - Each function in actions, keyed by action name, must return the new text of the main file, new contents of files of a folder document, new contents of companion files by extension, and the text of the _User_Action_Message_, each optional; a content is text, or `{ base64 }` for binary data; it must not write files itself.
  - `definePlugin` must reject a wrong definition with one line per wrong field, and the _Adoc_Server_ must validate every returned summary and action result the same way.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the _Adoc_Server_ writes the files returned by an action, so that _Document_Version_ checking stays in one place.
  - Chosen: the _Adoc_Server_ builds the _Document_Summary_List_ by calling summarize for each _Document_; a _Plugin_ has no separate list function.
  - Chosen: a thrown error becomes the parse error, so plugins need no try/catch.
}

concept _Plugin_Kit_ in plugin = {
  The package `@agent-workshop/adoc-plugin-kit`, the only package a _Plugin_ imports, which provides `definePlugin`, the `html` template, Markdown rendering with references and source positions, and helpers that write the _Anchor_Markup_Convention_.
.relations
  used by _Plugin_
  defines _Plugin_Interface_
  writes _Anchor_Markup_Convention_
  renders _Document_Reference_
  documented by _Plugin_Skill_
  styled by _Web_UI_Theme_
.contract
  - The _Plugin_Kit_ must provide a helper for every attribute of the _Anchor_Markup_Convention_, so that no plugin writes an attribute name by hand.
  - The `html` template of the _Plugin_Kit_ must escape every interpolated value except fragments it produced.
  - The Markdown rendering of the _Plugin_Kit_ must turn `[[KEY]]` and `[[KEY#anchor]]` into marked _Document_Reference_ links and must escape raw HTML.
  - The Markdown rendering of the _Plugin_Kit_ must mark the tokens of a fenced code block with syntax classes when the fence names a known language, and must mark a fenced block of the language `mermaid` as a diagram, keeping its escaped source.
  - The authoring guide of the _Plugin_Kit_ must contain a complete working plugin, the rules that avoid load errors, and the generic classes and design tokens of the _Web_UI_Theme_.
.remarks
  - Chosen: highlight.js marks code tokens with its `hljs-*` classes; the _Web_UI_Theme_ colours them.
  - Chosen: a plugin is one folder with `index.ts` and `guide.md`, loaded without a build step through Node's type stripping.
  - Chosen: the authoring guide is shown by `adoc skill view adoc-plugin-authoring`.
}

concept _Plugin_Directory_ in plugin = {
  A folder that holds _Plugin_ folders by name: `.adoc/plugins/` of the _Adoc_Workspace_ (project scope) and `adoc/plugins/` in the XDG config directory of the user, usually `~/.config/adoc/plugins/` (user scope).
.relations
  references _adoc:Adoc_Workspace_
  holds _Plugin_
  inside _Adoc_Home_
  read by _Adoc_Config_
  references _Agent_Skill_
.contract
  - A plugin source in the _Adoc_Config_ that is a bare name must be looked up as a folder of that name in the project _Plugin_Directory_ first, then in the user _Plugin_Directory_; a path and an npm package name keep working.
  - A _Plugin_ has the scope of the place it is loaded from: project when it is inside the _Adoc_Workspace_, user otherwise; its _Agent_Skill_ is installed in the same scope.
  - A _Plugin_ may have its own `package.json` with dependencies installed in its folder; it imports `@agent-workshop/adoc-plugin-kit` of the running adoc wherever its folder is.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the XDG base directory convention (`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, default `~/.config`).
}

concept _Plugin_Client_Module_ in plugin = {
  The folder `client/` of a _Plugin_ with an `index.js` (and optionally `index.css`) that the _Adoc_Web_UI_ loads, which defines the custom elements that the output of the _Plugin_Renderer_ uses for screens HTML alone cannot make, such as a drawing board.
.relations
  references _adoc:Document_
  part of _Plugin_
  loaded by _Adoc_Web_UI_
  served by _Adoc_Server_
  used by _Plugin_Renderer_
  sends _Document_Action_
  references _User_Comment_
  references _Document_Version_
.contract
  - The _Adoc_Server_ must serve the folder `client/` of every loaded _Plugin_ at `/assets/plugins/<plugin key>/`, and the _Adoc_Web_UI_ must load its `index.js` and `index.css` once.
  - An element of a _Plugin_Client_Module_ must change files only through a _Document_Action_: it dispatches the DOM event `adoc-action`, which the _Adoc_Web_UI_ sends with the shown _Document_Version_ and answers with the outcome.
  - An element may dispatch the DOM event `adoc-draft` to put one draft _User_Comment_ on its _Document_; a later one replaces it, so that the element has at most one draft per _Document_.
  - An element may read the main file of its _Document_ from `/api/documents/<key>/file` and must learn about changes from the window event `adoc-documents-changed`.
.remarks
  - Chosen: Web Components, so that the theme tokens, comments and anchors of the page work inside them.
  - Chosen: the plugin author bundles `client/index.js` with its libraries, so that no build tool runs in the _Adoc_Server_ and it works offline.
  - Chosen: the render output of such an element should stay the same across versions, so that the page does not replace the element and lose its state.
}

concept _Plugin_Key_ in plugin = {
  The identifier under which an _Adoc_Config_ uses a _Plugin_, written in uppercase letters only, such as TASK.
.relations
  identifies _Plugin_
  assigned by _Adoc_Config_
  unique within _Adoc_Workspace_
  prefixes _Document_Key_
.contract
  - A _Plugin_Key_ must consist of the uppercase letters A to Z only.
  - Each _Plugin_ in an _Adoc_Workspace_ must have a distinct _Plugin_Key_.
.remarks
  - Chosen: a _Plugin_Key_ has no hyphen, so the first hyphen of a _Document_Key_ always separates its parts.
}

concept _Plugin_Renderer_ in plugin = {
  The part of a _Plugin_ that renders one of its documents into an HTML string that becomes the body of a _Document_Detail_View_, marked by _Anchor_Markup_Convention_.
.relations
  part of _Plugin_
  renders body of _Document_Detail_View_
  follows _Anchor_Markup_Convention_
  marks _Document_Anchor_
  marks control of _Document_Action_
  recognizes _Document_Reference_
  parses _Document_
  runs on _Adoc_Server_
  output shown by _Adoc_Web_UI_
.contract
  - A _Plugin_Renderer_ must mark every _Document_Anchor_, every _Document_Reference_ and every control of a _Document_Action_ by _Anchor_Markup_Convention_.
  - A _Plugin_Renderer_ must recognize the _Document_Reference_ notation of its documents.
  - A _Plugin_Renderer_ must return an error message when it cannot parse a _Document_, and the _Adoc_Web_UI_ must show that error in place of the body.
  - A _Plugin_Renderer_ must run on the _Adoc_Server_ and return the body as an HTML string.
  - A _Plugin_Renderer_ must not ship scripts; every user operation must be a _Document_Action_ declared by _Anchor_Markup_Convention_.
.remarks
  - Chosen: plugin code runs only on the _Adoc_Server_, so plugins cannot diverge in browser behavior and stay cheap to write.
}

concept _Plugin_Action_Handler_ in plugin = {
  The part of a _Plugin_ that runs on the _Adoc_Server_ when a _Document_Action_ occurs, and that may change the _Document_, send a _User_Action_Message_, or both.
.relations
  part of _Plugin_
  handles _Document_Action_
  runs on _Adoc_Server_
  may change _Document_
  may send _User_Action_Message_
  checked against _Document_Version_
  replaced by _Default_Action_Handler_
  errors shown in _Adoc_Web_UI_
  leaves commit to _Assigned_Agent_
.contract
  - The _Adoc_Server_ must refuse to apply a change from a _Plugin_Action_Handler_ when the current _Document_Version_ differs from the one carried by the _Document_Action_, and the _Adoc_Web_UI_ must show the refusal.
  - A refused change must not send its _User_Action_Message_ either.
  - When a _Plugin_Action_Handler_ fails, the _Adoc_Web_UI_ must show the error, and nothing must be changed or sent.
  - A change made through a _Plugin_Action_Handler_ must stay uncommitted until the _Assigned_Agent_ commits.
.remarks
  - Example: clicking a TODO checkbox stores the done flag in the file and sends "TODO-gui#123 checked" to the agent.
  - Chosen: one path for every browser interaction. Program-driven changes and messages to the agent are two optional effects of the same handler, not two mechanisms.
  - Chosen: optimistic concurrency, so that a stale write never silently overwrites a change by the agent.
}

concept _Default_Action_Handler_ in plugin = {
  The handler of adoc itself that takes a _Document_Action_ that its _Plugin_ has no handler for, changes nothing, and sends a _User_Action_Message_ requesting the action.
.relations
  replaces _Plugin_Action_Handler_
  handles _Document_Action_
  sends _User_Action_Message_
  serves _Plugin_
  references _Document_
.contract
  - The _Default_Action_Handler_ must handle every _Document_Action_ whose name has no handler in the actions of its _Plugin_.
  - The _Default_Action_Handler_ must not change any _Document_.
  - The text of its _User_Action_Message_ must be `user request: <action name> <value>`, where the value of a toggle is the new checked state and the value of a drag is `<value> to <drop value>`.
.remarks
  - Example: the TASK status buttons have no handler and send "user request: set-status DONE".
}

concept _Plugin_Tab_ in plugin = {
  The _Adoc_Web_UI_ tab of one _Plugin_, made of its _Document_List_View_ and its _Document_Detail_View_.
.relations
  shows _Plugin_
  part of _Adoc_Web_UI_
  has_part _Document_List_View_
  has_part _Document_Detail_View_
.contract
  - An _Adoc_Web_UI_ must show one _Plugin_Tab_ per _Plugin_.
  - A _Plugin_Tab_ must show documents of its own _Plugin_ only.
}

concept _Agent_Skill_ in plugin = {
  A folder `skill/` with a `SKILL.md` in the Agent Skills format inside its owner folder: the core package (`adoc`, the assigned agent's workflow), the _Plugin_Kit_ (`adoc-plugin-authoring`) and each _Plugin_ (its _Plugin_Skill_).
.relations
  references _adoc:Adoc_Web_UI_
  references _adoc:Plugin_Skill_
  read by _Assigned_Agent_
  installed by _Skill_Install_Command_
  checked by _Skill_Check_
  shown by _Adoc_CLI_
  references _Plugin_Kit_
  references _Plugin_
.contract
  - Every _Agent_Skill_ must be the folder `skill/` of its owner folder, so that installing it never copies the owner's code.
  - `adoc skill view <name>` must show the `SKILL.md` of the _Agent_Skill_ with that name.
  - The _Adoc_Web_UI_ must show every _Agent_Skill_ read-only, rendered like a document body, so that the user reads what the agent reads.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the Agent Skills format (agentskills.io): a folder with `SKILL.md` whose front matter has `name` and `description`.
}

procedure _Skill_Install_Command_ in surface = {
  The `adoc skill install`, `adoc skill update` and `adoc skill uninstall` commands, which install every _Agent_Skill_ for the agents through the Vercel `skills` CLI (`npx skills add`).
.relations
  references _adoc:Plugin_
  references _adoc:Plugin_Kit_
  references _adoc:Plugin_Skill_
  part of _Adoc_CLI_
  installs _Agent_Skill_
  references _Plugin_Directory_
  references _Adoc_MCP_Tool_
.contract
  - `adoc skill install` must install the skills of the core package and the _Plugin_Kit_ in user scope, and the _Plugin_Skill_ of each _Plugin_ in the scope of that _Plugin_, by running `skills add <folder>`; `--agent` passes the agents on.
  - `adoc skill update` must do the same, replacing installed copies; `adoc skill uninstall` must remove every _Agent_Skill_ of the workspace through `skills remove`.
  - The _Adoc_MCP_Tool_ must refuse these commands.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the `skills` CLI writes the agent-specific places (`.agents/skills`, `.claude/skills`, …), so adoc supports every agent it supports.
  - Chosen: `ADOC_SKILLS_CLI` replaces the command (default `npx -y skills@1`), for internal mirrors and tests.
  - Chosen: whether `skills-lock.json` is committed is the user's decision.
}

procedure _Skill_Check_ in runtime = {
  Find every _Agent_Skill_ of the workspace that is not installed or whose installed copy differs from the one of the running adoc and its plugins.
.relations
  references _adoc:Adoc_Workspace_
  checks _Agent_Skill_
  run by _Adoc_CLI_
  run by _Adoc_Check_Command_
  run by _Adoc_Server_
  references _Skill_Install_Command_
.contract
  - _Skill_Check_ must look for each _Agent_Skill_ by name in `.agents/skills` and `.claude/skills` of the _Adoc_Workspace_ and of the user's home, and report it as missing when none has it, or as outdated when its `SKILL.md` differs from the source.
  - Each finding must be a warning that names the skill and suggests `adoc skill install` or `adoc skill update`.
.remarks
  - Chosen: "differs" compares the `SKILL.md` text, so no version field has to be kept in step.
}

concept _Plugin_Skill_ in plugin = {
  The _Agent_Skill_ in which a _Plugin_ tells the _Assigned_Agent_ how to work with its documents: `skill/SKILL.md` in the folder of the _Plugin_, named in its front matter, such as `adoc-todo`.
.relations
  part of _Plugin_
  is_a _Agent_Skill_
  read by _Assigned_Agent_
  shown by _Adoc_CLI_
  explains _Document_Anchor_
  explains _Document_Local_ID_
  explains _Document_Action_
  explains _User_Action_Message_
  explains _Plugin_Action_Handler_
.contract
  - A _Plugin_ must have its _Plugin_Skill_ at `skill/SKILL.md` next to its `index.ts`; a _Plugin_ without it fails to load.
  - A _Plugin_Skill_ must explain the file layout and format of the documents of its _Plugin_.
  - A _Plugin_Skill_ must let the agent locate any _Document_Anchor_ of its _Plugin_ in the files.
  - A _Plugin_Skill_ must state the recommended form of a new _Document_Local_ID_.
  - A _Plugin_Skill_ must list each _Document_Action_ name of its _Plugin_, what its _Plugin_Action_Handler_ already does, and what the agent is expected to do on the resulting _User_Action_Message_.
}

concept _Document_ in document = {
  One unit of content of one _Plugin_, stored as one file or one folder in an _Adoc_Workspace_ and identified by one _Document_Key_.
.relations
  references _adoc:Adoc_Server_
  references _adoc:Document_Action_
  defined by _Plugin_
  identified by _Document_Key_
  versioned by _Document_Version_
  stored in _Adoc_Workspace_
  changed by _Assigned_Agent_
  changed by _Plugin_Action_Handler_
  shown in _Adoc_Web_UI_
.contract
  - The file or folder name of a _Document_ must be its _Document_Key_, followed by the file extension when it is a file, such as `TASK-1231.md` or `BUG-42/`.
  - Every file inside the folder of a folder _Document_ must belong to that _Document_.
  - A file _Document_ may have companion files: files next to it with the same name and another extension that its _Plugin_ declares, such as `SKETCH-login.png` beside `SKETCH-login.excalidraw`; they belong to the _Document_, count for its _Document_Version_ and its last update, and move with it.
  - The git copy of a _Document_ must be its source of truth.
  - A _Document_ must change only through the _Assigned_Agent_, a _Plugin_Action_Handler_, an edit of its main file in the _Adoc_Web_UI_, or a direct file edit.
  - An _Adoc_Web_UI_ must not write any file of a _Document_ itself: it sends a _Document_Action_ or the edited main file to the _Adoc_Server_, which writes it after checking the _Document_Version_.
.remarks
  - Chosen: direct file edits by people are allowed but not recommended.
}

concept _Document_Version_ in document = {
  A hash of the contents of a _Document_ that changes whenever any of its files changes, used to detect stale writes.
.relations
  versions _Document_
  carried by _Document_Action_
  guards _Plugin_Action_Handler_
.contract
  - The _Document_Version_ of a file _Document_ must be the hash of the file contents.
  - The _Document_Version_ of a folder _Document_ must be the hash of the relative paths and contents of all its files.
  - The _Document_Version_ must not depend on file times.
}

concept _Document_Key_ in document = {
  The canonical identifier of a _Document_, made of its _Plugin_Key_, a hyphen and its _Document_Local_ID_, such as TASK-1231.
.relations
  identifies _Document_
  composed of _Plugin_Key_
  composed of _Document_Local_ID_
  written in _Document_Reference_
  written in _User_Message_
  shown in _Adoc_Web_UI_
  checked by _Duplicate_Document_Key_Warning_
.contract
  - A _Document_Key_ must be the only written form of a document identity, in file names, in a _Document_Reference_, in a _User_Message_ and in the _Adoc_Web_UI_.
  - The first hyphen of a _Document_Key_ must separate the _Plugin_Key_ from the _Document_Local_ID_.
}

concept _Document_Local_ID_ in document = {
  The part of a _Document_Key_ after its first hyphen, which distinguishes documents within one _Plugin_, such as 260930-order-paging or gui.
.relations
  part of _Document_Key_
  distinguishes _Document_
  unique within _Plugin_
  explained by _Plugin_Skill_
.contract
  - A _Document_Local_ID_ must use only lowercase letters, digits, hyphens, underscores and dots.
  - A _Document_Local_ID_ must be unique within its _Plugin_.
  - adoc must not generate a _Document_Local_ID_; the user or agent that creates the _Document_ chooses it.
.remarks
  - Chosen: lowercase only, so that case-insensitive file systems cannot merge two documents.
  - Chosen: Korean or other non-ASCII titles are not allowed; a title is written in English words.
  - Chosen: the recommended forms are a date and a title (yymmdd-title) or a title alone, because sequential numbers collide across git branches. Sequential numbers are acceptable for solo work.
  - Chosen: an individual _Plugin_ may still offer a numbering function of its own.
}

concept _Document_Anchor_ in document = {
  A position inside a _Document_ that a _User_Message_ can target, written after a hash sign that follows the _Document_Key_, such as TODO-gui#123.
.relations
  points into _Document_
  appended to _Document_Key_
  form decided by _Plugin_
  explained by _Plugin_Skill_
  targeted by _User_Message_
.contract
  - A _Document_Anchor_ must be written as the _Document_Key_, a hash sign and the anchor value.
  - The form of a _Document_Anchor_ value must be decided by the _Plugin_ of its _Document_.
.remarks
  - Example: a line number for a Markdown source, a key path for a YAML or JSON source, or an item id.
  - Chosen: the agent understands the anchor through the _Plugin_Skill_; adoc does not interpret it.
}

concept _Anchor_Markup_Convention_ in document = {
  The rule by which a _Plugin_Renderer_ marks rendered elements with data attributes so that the _Adoc_Web_UI_ can recognize anchors, source positions, references and each _Document_Action_.
.relations
  references _adoc:Document_
  references _adoc:Document_Detail_View_
  followed by _Plugin_Renderer_
  written by _Plugin_Kit_
  read by _Adoc_Web_UI_
  marks _Document_Anchor_
  marks _Document_Reference_
  carries _Document_Key_
  declares _Document_Action_
  supplies position to _User_Comment_
.contract
  - A rendered element of a _Document_Anchor_ must carry the anchor value in `data-adoc-anchor`.
  - A rendered element may carry its source position, written as `file:line`, in `data-adoc-source`, and the _Adoc_Web_UI_ must put the nearest one into a _User_Comment_ on that element or text.
  - A rendered _Document_Reference_ must carry the referenced _Document_Key_, optionally with `#anchor`, in `data-adoc-ref`.
  - A rendered control of a _Document_Action_ must carry the action name in `data-adoc-action`, the kind in `data-adoc-kind` and the value in `data-adoc-value`.
  - A drop zone of a drag action must carry the action name in `data-adoc-drop` and its value in `data-adoc-drop-value`.
  - A rendered control of a _Document_Action_ may carry in `data-adoc-confirm` a question that the _Adoc_Web_UI_ asks the user before it sends the action, such as when the action asks the agent to start work.
.remarks
  - Chosen: data attributes rather than class names, because class names serve styling.
  - Chosen: the body never carries the _Document_Key_ itself, because a _Document_Detail_View_ shows one _Document_ and its frame knows the key.
}

concept _Document_Action_ in document = {
  A user operation on a control in the body of a _Document_Detail_View_, declared by _Anchor_Markup_Convention_ and handled by a _Plugin_Action_Handler_ or the _Default_Action_Handler_.
.relations
  declared by _Anchor_Markup_Convention_
  occurs in _Document_Detail_View_
  handled by _Plugin_Action_Handler_
  handled by _Default_Action_Handler_
  sent by _Adoc_Web_UI_
  received by _Adoc_Server_
  carries _Document_Version_
  may carry _Document_Anchor_
.contract
  - A _Document_Action_ must be one of the kinds click, toggle and drag-and-drop.
  - A new kind of _Document_Action_ must be added to _Anchor_Markup_Convention_ for all plugins, never inside one plugin.
  - An _Adoc_Web_UI_ must send each _Document_Action_ to the _Adoc_Server_ with its kind, its name, its value, the new checked state for a toggle, the drop value for a drag, its _Document_Anchor_ if any, and the _Document_Version_ that was rendered.
  - A click on a control of a _Document_Action_ must never start a comment; commenting on an element must use a separate comment control of the _Adoc_Web_UI_.
.remarks
  - Chosen: click, toggle and drag-and-drop cover the TODO, TASK and KANBAN plugins.
}

concept _Document_Reference_ in document = {
  A link written in the content of one _Document_ that points to another _Document_, or to a _Document_Anchor_ in it, by its _Document_Key_, such as `[[TASK-1231]]` in Markdown.
.relations
  points to _Document_
  may point to _Document_Anchor_
  written with _Document_Key_
  crosses _Plugin_
  notation recognized by _Plugin_Renderer_
  resolved by _Document_Reference_Resolution_
  checked by _Broken_Document_Reference_Warning_
  shows _Document_Summary_
  shown in _Adoc_Web_UI_
.contract
  - A _Document_Reference_ may point to a _Document_ of any _Plugin_.
  - The notation of a _Document_Reference_ must be recognized by the _Plugin_Renderer_ of the containing _Document_.
  - An _Adoc_Web_UI_ must show the _Document_Summary_ of the referenced _Document_ as the tooltip of a _Document_Reference_, and must open that _Document_ when the reference is followed.
.remarks
  - Chosen: a _Document_Reference_ is a function of adoc itself, so it does not mix plugins.
  - Chosen: the recommended notation in Markdown is the _Document_Key_ enclosed in double square brackets; a _Plugin_Renderer_ may define another notation, including for YAML or JSON values.
  - Chosen: pointing to a _Document_Anchor_, such as TASK-1231#method, is desirable but optional.
}

concept _Document_Summary_ in document = {
  The small object that the summarize function of a _Plugin_ returns for one _Document_, made of its title, its status and any free fields.
.relations
  describes _Document_
  returned by _Plugin_
  shown in _Adoc_Web_UI_
.contract
  - A _Document_Summary_ must contain a title and a status.
  - A _Document_Summary_ may contain free fields, and the _Adoc_Web_UI_ must show them as a table.
  - The status of a _Document_Summary_ must be free text that adoc shows as is and never interprets.
.remarks
  - Example: a tooltip reading "Improve xyz service (DONE)" above a table of the free fields.
  - Chosen: no common status category for now.
}

concept _Document_Summary_List_ in document = {
  The list that the _Adoc_Server_ builds for one _Plugin_ with one entry for each of its documents, which is the _Document_Summary_ or, when summarize fails, the _Document_Key_ with the parse error, together with the last update of the document.
.relations
  built by _Adoc_Server_
  has_member _Document_Summary_
  covers _Document_
  covers _Watch_Path_
  for _Plugin_
  shows _Document_Key_
  used by _Document_List_View_
  references _Assigned_Agent_
  references _Document_Archive_
.contract
  - A _Document_Summary_List_ must contain exactly one entry for each _Document_ of its _Plugin_ under every _Watch_Path_.
  - An entry whose summarize failed must show the _Document_Key_ and the parse error instead of a _Document_Summary_.
  - Every entry, also one whose summarize failed, must carry the last update of its _Document_: the newest modification time of its files.
  - Every entry must say whether its _Document_ is in a _Document_Archive_.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the last update is the file modification time, not the last git commit, so that an edit by the _Assigned_Agent_ shows at once.
}

concept _Document_List_View_ in document = {
  The part of a _Plugin_Tab_ that the _Adoc_Web_UI_ renders as a plain list of the documents of its _Plugin_ from a _Document_Summary_List_.
.relations
  part of _Plugin_Tab_
  rendered by _Adoc_Web_UI_
  lists _Plugin_
  uses _Document_Summary_List_
  references _Plugin_Renderer_
.contract
  - A _Document_List_View_ must be rendered by the _Adoc_Web_UI_ alone, without a _Plugin_Renderer_.
}

concept _Document_Detail_View_ in document = {
  The part of a _Plugin_Tab_ that shows one _Document_, with a frame rendered by the _Adoc_Web_UI_ around a body rendered by the _Plugin_Renderer_.
.relations
  part of _Plugin_Tab_
  hosted by _Adoc_Web_UI_
  body rendered by _Plugin_Renderer_
  shows _Document_
  frame shows _Document_Key_
  frame shows _Document_Summary_
  frame shows _Document_Reference_
  comments on _Document_Anchor_
  collects _User_Comment_
  reads _Anchor_Markup_Convention_
  contains _Document_Action_
  sends to _Adoc_Server_
.contract
  - The body of a _Document_Detail_View_ must be the HTML string returned by the _Plugin_Renderer_.
  - The _Adoc_Web_UI_ must render the frame around the body: the header with the _Document_Key_ and the title and status from the _Document_Summary_, a comment control on each marked _Document_Anchor_, a comment input on selected text that adds a draft _User_Comment_, the tooltip and broken mark of each _Document_Reference_, and errors and warnings.
  - The _Adoc_Web_UI_ must send every _Document_Action_ in the body to the _Adoc_Server_.
}

concept _User_Message_ in message = {
  A one-time message to the _Assigned_Agent_ about something the user did in the _Adoc_Web_UI_, either a _User_Comment_Message_ composed in the _Adoc_Web_UI_ or a _User_Action_Message_ produced by a handler on the _Adoc_Server_.
.relations
  originates in _Adoc_Web_UI_
  held by _Adoc_Server_
  delivered to _Assigned_Agent_
  delivered by _User_Message_Transport_
  written in _User_Message_Format_
  aims at _User_Message_Target_
  has_member _User_Comment_Message_
  has_member _User_Action_Message_
  names _Document_Key_
  names _Document_Anchor_
  references _User_Comment_
.contract
  - A _User_Message_ must be either a _User_Comment_Message_ or a _User_Action_Message_.
  - An _Adoc_Server_ must hold a _User_Message_ until the _User_Message_Transport_ delivers it, and must forget it after delivery.
  - An _Adoc_Server_ must deliver held messages in the order they were created.
  - An _Adoc_Web_UI_ must show every _User_Message_ that has not been delivered yet.
  - A _User_Action_Message_ and each _User_Comment_ of a _User_Comment_Message_ must name its _User_Message_Target_ by _Document_Key_ and _Document_Anchor_ where the target level has them.
.remarks
  - Chosen: a _User_Message_ is equivalent to input typed into the agent's chat.
  - Chosen: the agent reacts by editing documents or doing the requested work.
  - Chosen: there is no channel from the agent back to the user for now; the user watches the agent window. Copying the herdr window into the web UI may be considered later.
  - Chosen: held messages may be lost when the _Adoc_Server_ restarts.
}

concept _User_Comment_Message_ in message = {
  A _User_Message_ that carries the text the user typed in the composer, about one _User_Message_Target_, together with the _User_Comment_ entries the user collected as drafts, all sent at once.
.relations
  is_a _User_Message_
  composed in _Adoc_Web_UI_
  aims at _User_Message_Target_
  has_member _User_Comment_
.contract
  - A _User_Comment_Message_ must carry composer text, with its _User_Message_Target_, or at least one _User_Comment_, or both.
  - The _User_Comment_ entries of a _User_Comment_Message_ must keep the order in which the user added them.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the composer text is the main message and the drafts are attachments to it, like a chat message with annotations.
  - Chosen: drafts are collected and sent together, like the comments of one code review, so that the agent handles related requests in one turn.
  - Chosen: attachments of files are not supported for now.
}

concept _User_Comment_ in message = {
  One comment inside a _User_Comment_Message_: text about one _User_Message_Target_, with the selected text and source position when there are any.
.relations
  member of _User_Comment_Message_
  aims at _User_Message_Target_
  carries _User_Comment_Quote_
  position from _Anchor_Markup_Convention_
  about _Document_
  about _Plugin_
.contract
  - A _User_Comment_ must carry its _User_Message_Target_ and non-empty text.
  - A _User_Comment_ must carry the _User_Comment_Quote_ when the user selected text.
  - A _User_Comment_ must carry the source position when the commented element or text carries one.
}

concept _User_Comment_Quote_ in message = {
  The text the user selected by dragging in a _Document_Detail_View_, carried in a _User_Comment_ so that the agent can find the position even after the _Document_ has changed.
.relations
  carried by _User_Comment_
  selected in _Document_Detail_View_
  locates text in _Document_
  references _Document_Version_
.remarks
  - Chosen: no _Document_Version_ is carried; the agent locates the position by the quote.
}

concept _User_Action_Message_ in message = {
  A _User_Message_ that a _Plugin_Action_Handler_ or the _Default_Action_Handler_ produces to tell the agent about a _Document_Action_, either as a request or as a notice of a change already made.
.relations
  is_a _User_Message_
  produced by _Plugin_Action_Handler_
  produced by _Default_Action_Handler_
  reports _Document_Action_
  may report change of _Document_
.contract
  - A _User_Action_Message_ must carry the action name, its value and the text written by its handler.
  - A _User_Action_Message_ must state whether its handler has already changed the _Document_.
}

concept _User_Message_Target_ in message = {
  What a _User_Message_ is about, at one of five levels: the whole _Adoc_Workspace_, one _Plugin_, one _Document_, one _Document_Anchor_ or one _Agent_Skill_.
.relations
  scope of _User_Message_
  may be _Adoc_Workspace_
  may be _Plugin_
  may be _Document_
  may be _Document_Anchor_
  may be _Agent_Skill_
  composed in _Adoc_Web_UI_
  composed as _User_Comment_
.contract
  - A _User_Message_Target_ must be exactly one of the workspace, plugin, document, anchor and skill levels.
  - An _Adoc_Web_UI_ must let the user give a _User_Comment_ any of the five levels.
.remarks
  - Example: "create a new issue" targets a _Plugin_ because no _Document_ exists yet.
}

concept _User_Message_Format_ in message = {
  The text form in which every _User_Message_ reaches the agent: a header line, the main text, and the attached fields in YAML after a line `--`.
.relations
  references _adoc:Agent_Skill_
  fields from _Adoc_Web_UI_
  formats _User_Message_
  used by _User_Message_Transport_
  used by _User_Message_Wait_Command_
  names _User_Message_Target_
  lists _User_Comment_
  includes _User_Comment_Quote_
  states target with _Document_Key_
  states target with _Plugin_Key_
  states target with _Document_Anchor_
  reports change of _Document_
  run of _Adoc_Server_
.contract
  - A message in _User_Message_Format_ must start with the line `[adoc message <number>] <kind>`, followed by ` · <target>` when the message has a main target; kind is comment or action and the number increases within one run of the _Adoc_Server_.
  - A target in _User_Message_Format_ must be written as `workspace`, a _Plugin_Key_, a _Document_Key_, a _Document_Key_ with a _Document_Anchor_, or `skill <name>` for an _Agent_Skill_.
  - The main text must follow the header line as plain text: the composer text of a comment message, or the handler text of an action message.
  - Attached fields must follow a line `--` as YAML: for a comment message the field comments, a list with one entry per _User_Comment_ with target and text and, when present, quote and source; for an action message the fields action, value and applied, and to for a drag.
  - A comment message without composer text must start its body with the line `--`; a comment message without drafts must have no `--` part.
  - With `--output json` or `--output yaml`, the same content must be returned as structured data.
.remarks
  - Example of a comment: `[adoc message 3] comment · TASK-261002-herdr-integration`, the composer text, then `--` and `comments:` with entries such as `- target: TASK-1231#method`, `source: docs/tasks/TASK-1231.md:19`, `quote: infinite scroll`, `text: use page numbers instead`.
  - Example of an action: `[adoc message 4] action · TODO-gui#3`, `user request: do item TODO-gui#3: Refactor PaymentRepo`, then `--`, `action: toggle`, `value: "3"`, `applied: false`.
  - Chosen: the user's words come first and the machine fields last, so that a pushed prompt reads like a chat message.
  - Chosen: the plugin writes only the text of an action; adoc writes every other field, because those come from the _Adoc_Web_UI_.
}

concept _User_Message_Transport_ in message = {
  The integration through which a _User_Message_ reaches the _Assigned_Agent_, configured in _Adoc_Config_ and kept separate from the message content.
.relations
  delivers _User_Message_
  delivers to _Assigned_Agent_
  configured by _Adoc_Config_
  uses _User_Message_Format_
  uses _Agent_Claim_
  has_part _User_Message_Wait_Command_
.contract
  - All kinds of _User_Message_Transport_ must share one interface, so that a new kind can be added without changing the rest of adoc.
  - adoc must provide the herdr and wait kinds of _User_Message_Transport_.
  - The herdr kind of _User_Message_Transport_ must be the default; it must deliver to the pane named by the _Agent_Claim_, with `agent.prompt`, or as typed input followed by Enter while herdr has not detected an agent in that pane.
  - While the herdr kind has no _Agent_Claim_, every _User_Message_ must stay held, so that `adoc message wait` can still take it.
  - Every kind of _User_Message_Transport_ must deliver the same text in _User_Message_Format_.
  - A push kind, such as herdr, must deliver each _User_Message_ as soon as it is created, and must keep it held when delivery fails.
}

concept _Adoc_Server_ in runtime = {
  The local adoc process of one _Adoc_Workspace_ that loads plugins, watches files, writes changes returned by handlers, serves the _Adoc_Web_UI_ and the _Adoc_MCP_Tool_, and holds every _User_Message_ until delivery.
.relations
  references _adoc:Document_Version_
  serves _Adoc_Workspace_
  configured by _Adoc_Config_
  loads _Plugin_
  watches _Watch_Path_
  builds _Document_Summary_List_
  serves _Adoc_Web_UI_
  serves _Adoc_MCP_Tool_
  holds _User_Message_
  started by _Adoc_CLI_
  writes _Server_Record_
  tracks _Browser_Session_
  relays _Agent_Terminal_Stream_
  watches _Agent_Claim_
  keeps _Document_Version_Store_
.contract
  - An _Adoc_Server_ must run locally, one per _Adoc_Workspace_, in the foreground of `adoc server run` or inside `adoc mcp run --with-server`.
  - An _Adoc_Server_ must accept remote connections within an internal network without authentication.
  - An _Adoc_Server_ that listens on an address other than loopback must warn when it starts that anyone who reaches it can read and edit the documents and control the agent's terminal.
  - An _Adoc_Server_ must refuse to start on a port that is already in use.
  - An _Adoc_Server_ must write its _Server_Record_ when it starts and remove it when it stops, and must refuse to start while the _Server_Record_ of the same _Adoc_Workspace_ names a running process.
  - An _Adoc_Server_ must reload a _Plugin_ loaded from a local path whenever a file at the top of its folder, such as `index.ts`, changes, and refresh the _Adoc_Web_UI_.
  - An _Adoc_Server_ must write an edited main file or `SKILL.md` sent by the _Adoc_Web_UI_ only when the version it was edited from is still current, and must answer with the new version and the unified diff from the text the edit started from.
  - An _Adoc_Server_ must remove scripts and inline event attributes from every body HTML before serving it.
.remarks
  - Chosen: implemented in TypeScript.
  - Chosen: plugin reloading shortens the loop of writing a plugin to editing `index.ts` and looking at the page.
  - Non-goal: authentication.
}

concept _Adoc_Web_UI_ in runtime = {
  The browser interface served by the _Adoc_Server_ where the user reads rendered documents, composes a _User_Comment_Message_ and triggers each _Document_Action_.
.relations
  served by _Adoc_Server_
  has_part _Plugin_Tab_
  composes _User_Comment_Message_
  collects _User_Comment_
  sends _Document_Action_
.contract
  - An _Adoc_Web_UI_ must offer one composer, outside every _Plugin_Tab_, that sends the collected draft _User_Comment_ entries and an optional comment on the current target as one _User_Comment_Message_.
  - An _Adoc_Web_UI_ must keep draft _User_Comment_ entries across navigation until they are sent or removed.
}

concept _Web_UI_Theme_ in runtime = {
  The visual system of the _Adoc_Web_UI_, taken from the "opencode" theme of the opencode TUI: design tokens for surface, text, status, diff, Markdown and syntax colours in a light and a dark variant, the accent bar, the type scale, the bundled fonts and the icons.
.relations
  references _adoc:Adoc_Config_
  styles _Adoc_Web_UI_
  styles _Plugin_Kit_
  offered to _Plugin_
.contract
  - The _Web_UI_Theme_ must define every colour as a design token, a CSS custom property named `--adoc-*`, with the values of the opencode theme in a light and a dark variant; components and plugins must use the tokens instead of colour literals.
  - The _Web_UI_Theme_ must separate regions by three surface levels (surface, panel, element) rather than borders, and must mark emphasis such as selection, focus, a held message or a warning with an accent bar on the left edge.
  - The _Web_UI_Theme_ must draw every box with square corners, so that an accent bar stays a straight line.
  - In the _Web_UI_Theme_ the largest text must be the base body size; headings must stand out by colour and weight, and only smaller sizes are allowed for meta information.
  - The _Web_UI_Theme_ must show the default colour scheme of the _Adoc_Config_ from the first paint, unless the user chose system, light or dark in this browser, and must remember that choice per browser.
  - The _Web_UI_Theme_ must bundle its fonts so that the _Adoc_Web_UI_ looks the same offline: a proportional font with Hangul for text and a monospace font with Hangul and Nerd Font symbols for terminals and code.
  - The _Web_UI_Theme_ must draw icons as vector graphics.
  - The _Web_UI_Theme_ must style the generic `adoc-*` classes listed in the authoring guide of the _Plugin_Kit_, so that a plugin needs no CSS of its own.
.remarks
  - Chosen: tokens and colours from `packages/tui/src/theme/assets/opencode.json` of opencode; Markdown and syntax colours from the same file.
  - Chosen: Pretendard for text; D2Coding with Symbols Nerd Font Mono for terminals and code; Lucide icons.
  - Chosen: "chip" is the one name for a small label; there is no separate badge.
}

procedure _User_Message_Wait_Command_ in message = {
  The `adoc message wait` command with which the _Assigned_Agent_ blocks until at least one _User_Message_ is held, then receives every held message.
.relations
  part of _Adoc_CLI_
  invoked by _Assigned_Agent_
  returns _User_Message_
  uses _User_Message_Format_
  part of _User_Message_Transport_
  needs _Adoc_Server_
.contract
  - _User_Message_Wait_Command_ must return all held messages in creation order, each in _User_Message_Format_, and the _Adoc_Server_ must treat them as delivered.
  - _User_Message_Wait_Command_ must return with no message when the `--timeout` option expires.
  - _User_Message_Wait_Command_ must fail with a clear error when no _Adoc_Server_ is running.
.remarks
  - Chosen: `adoc message list` shows held messages without delivering them.
}

procedure _Adoc_Check_Command_ in runtime = {
  The `adoc check` command that reports every warning and error of an _Adoc_Workspace_ without changing anything.
.relations
  part of _Adoc_CLI_
  checks _Adoc_Workspace_
  runs _Duplicate_Document_Key_Warning_
  runs _Broken_Document_Reference_Warning_
  reports parse errors of _Document_
  reports load errors of _Plugin_
  reports names under _Watch_Path_
  compares with _Plugin_Key_
  output repeated by _Adoc_Server_
.contract
  - _Adoc_Check_Command_ must report duplicate document keys, broken document references, documents that fail to parse and plugins that fail to load.
  - _Adoc_Check_Command_ must report a file under a _Watch_Path_ whose name looks like a document key but whose prefix is not a declared _Plugin_Key_.
  - _Adoc_Check_Command_ must report a warning when the _Adoc_Workspace_ is not inside a git repository.
  - _Adoc_Check_Command_ must exit with a nonzero status when it reports an error.
  - An _Adoc_Server_ must print the same report when it starts.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the agent runs it after editing, like `aterm corpus check`.
}

procedure _Document_Change_Notification_ in runtime = {
  Detect the creation, change, deletion or renaming of a file under a _Watch_Path_, find the owning _Document_ and _Plugin_, and refresh the _Adoc_Web_UI_.
.relations
  run by _Adoc_Server_
  watches _Watch_Path_
  finds _Document_
  notifies _Plugin_
  owner found by _Plugin_Key_
  refreshes _Adoc_Web_UI_
  updates _Document_Summary_List_
  reacts to _Plugin_Action_Handler_
  preserves draft of _User_Comment_
.contract
  - _Document_Change_Notification_ must find the owning _Plugin_ from the _Plugin_Key_ at the start of the file or folder name.
  - _Document_Change_Notification_ must react to direct file edits as well as to edits by the agent and by a _Plugin_Action_Handler_.
  - _Document_Change_Notification_ must update the _Document_Summary_List_ when a _Document_ is created, deleted or renamed.
  - _Document_Change_Notification_ must keep, as far as possible, the user's text selection and every draft _User_Comment_ not yet sent when the _Adoc_Web_UI_ re-renders.
}

procedure _Document_Reference_Resolution_ in document = {
  Find the _Document_ that a _Document_Reference_ points to and return its _Document_Summary_ from its _Plugin_.
.relations
  resolves _Document_Reference_
  finds _Document_
  reads _Document_Key_
  selects by _Plugin_Key_
  asks _Plugin_
  returns _Document_Summary_
  reports to _Broken_Document_Reference_Warning_
.contract
  - _Document_Reference_Resolution_ must select the _Plugin_ by the _Plugin_Key_ of the referenced _Document_Key_.
  - _Document_Reference_Resolution_ must report a missing _Document_ instead of returning a _Document_Summary_.
}

procedure _Duplicate_Document_Key_Warning_ in runtime = {
  Warn the user when two files or folders under the watch paths carry the same _Document_Key_.
.relations
  run by _Adoc_Server_
  run by _Adoc_Check_Command_
  checks _Document_Key_
  covers _Watch_Path_
  shown in _Adoc_Web_UI_
.contract
  - _Duplicate_Document_Key_Warning_ must show a warning in the _Adoc_Web_UI_ that names every conflicting file or folder.
}

procedure _Broken_Document_Reference_Warning_ in runtime = {
  Warn the user when a _Document_Reference_ points to a _Document_ that does not exist.
.relations
  run by _Adoc_Server_
  run by _Adoc_Check_Command_
  checks _Document_Reference_
  uses _Document_Reference_Resolution_
  detects missing _Document_
  shown in _Adoc_Web_UI_
.contract
  - _Broken_Document_Reference_Warning_ must mark each broken _Document_Reference_ where the _Adoc_Web_UI_ shows it.
}

concept _Server_Record_ in runtime = {
  The small file outside the _Adoc_Workspace_, in the runtime directory of the computer, in which a running _Adoc_Server_ records its process id, URL and workspace.
.relations
  written by _Adoc_Server_
  read by _Adoc_CLI_
  names _Adoc_Workspace_
.contract
  - A _Server_Record_ must be keyed by the absolute path of its _Adoc_Workspace_, so that one computer runs at most one _Adoc_Server_ per workspace.
  - A _Server_Record_ whose process no longer runs must be treated as absent.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the record lives in `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/adoc/`, or the system temporary directory, never in the repository.
}

concept _Browser_Session_ in runtime = {
  One browser tab of the _Adoc_Web_UI_ connected to the _Adoc_Server_, identified by an id that the tab keeps for its lifetime.
.relations
  connects to _Adoc_Server_
  part of _Adoc_Web_UI_
  moved by _Browser_Open_Command_
.contract
  - An _Adoc_Server_ must track for each _Browser_Session_ its id, whether it is connected, the time of its last access and its current location.
  - The last access of a _Browser_Session_ must be updated on every navigation, click, key press and focus in that tab.
  - A _Browser_Session_ must survive a reload of its tab and keep its id.
.remarks
  - Chosen: sessions are kept in memory and forgotten when the _Adoc_Server_ restarts.
}

concept _Document_Archive_ in document = {
  Every folder named `_archive` inside a _Watch_Path_; a _Document_ inside one, at any depth, is archived: kept with its _Document_Key_ but out of the way.
.relations
  references _adoc:Plugin_
  inside _Watch_Path_
  holds _Document_
  references _Document_Key_
  references _Document_Reference_
  references _Plugin_Tab_
  references _Assigned_Agent_
  references _Default_Action_Handler_
  references _Duplicate_Document_Key_Warning_
  references _Document_Find_Command_
.contract
  - An archived _Document_ must keep its _Document_Key_, so that every _Document_Reference_ to it still resolves.
  - When an archived and a not archived _Document_ carry the same _Document_Key_, the not archived one must be used, and the _Duplicate_Document_Key_Warning_ must name both.
  - The document count of a _Plugin_Tab_ must leave archived documents out.
  - The _Assigned_Agent_ archives a _Document_ by moving it with `git mv` into an `_archive` folder next to it, and restores it by moving it back; adoc itself never moves documents, and an archive request from the user reaches the agent through the _Default_Action_Handler_ as the actions `archive` and `unarchive`.
  - The _Document_Find_Command_ must leave archived documents out unless `--archived` asks for them.
.remarks
  - Chosen: a folder rather than a status field, so that one mechanism works for every _Plugin_, also for those without a status.
  - Chosen: the leading underscore marks a folder that adoc treats specially, as in `_drafts` of Jekyll.
  - Example: `docs/tasks/_archive/TASK-261002-ui-polish.md` is the archived TASK-261002-ui-polish.
}

procedure _Document_Find_Command_ in surface = {
  The `adoc document list` and `adoc document search <text>` commands with which the _Assigned_Agent_ finds documents without reading archived ones.
.relations
  references _adoc:Document_Key_
  part of _Adoc_CLI_
  invoked by _Assigned_Agent_
  lists _Document_
  uses _Document_Summary_List_
  references _Document_Archive_
  references _Plugin_Key_
.contract
  - `adoc document list` must show the _Document_Key_, title, status, last update and path of each _Document_, newest first, optionally of one _Plugin_Key_ with `--plugin`.
  - `adoc document search <text>` must show each line of a _Document_ file that contains the text, case-insensitive, as key, path, line number and line, optionally of one _Plugin_Key_ with `--plugin`.
  - Both must leave archived documents out by default and show only archived ones with `--archived`.
.remarks
  - Chosen: `--archived` means "only archived", the same as the archive button of the web UI; run both forms to see everything.
  - Chosen: the agent guide tells the agent to find documents with these commands rather than `ls` or `grep`, so that archived documents do not fill its context.
}

procedure _Browser_Open_Command_ in surface = {
  The `adoc ui open` command with which the _Assigned_Agent_ sends a _Browser_Session_ to a _Document_, a _Document_Anchor_ or a _Plugin_; `adoc ui list` lists the sessions.
.relations
  part of _Adoc_CLI_
  invoked by _Assigned_Agent_
  moves _Browser_Session_
  opens _Document_
  opens _Document_Anchor_
  opens _Plugin_
.contract
  - _Browser_Open_Command_ must send the connected _Browser_Session_ with the latest last access, unless `--session` names another.
  - _Browser_Open_Command_ must fail with a clear error when no _Browser_Session_ is connected.
  - `adoc ui list` must show each _Browser_Session_ with its id, connection state, last access and location, most recent first.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the name follows `aterm ui`.
  - Example: after writing a NOTE, the agent runs `adoc ui open NOTE-261002-note-plugin` so that the user sees it.
}

concept _Document_Version_Store_ in runtime = {
  The memory in which the _Adoc_Server_ keeps the files of recent versions of each _Document_, so that the changes since an earlier _Document_Version_ can be shown.
.relations
  references _adoc:Adoc_Web_UI_
  references _adoc:Document_
  kept by _Adoc_Server_
  stores _Document_Version_
  feeds _Plugin_Interface_
.contract
  - The _Document_Version_Store_ must keep at least the last twenty versions of each _Document_ seen since the _Adoc_Server_ started.
  - A request for the changes of a _Document_ must name the base _Document_Version_; when the store no longer holds it, the _Adoc_Web_UI_ must say that the changes are unavailable.
  - The _Document_Version_Store_ must list the versions it holds for a _Document_, newest first, each with the time it was first seen.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the default base is the version the browser showed last, so the user sees everything that changed since they last looked; any other version in the store can be chosen.
  - Chosen: memory only, so changes from before a restart are not available; git keeps the full history.
}

concept _Agent_Claim_ in workspace = {
  The record, in the file `.adoc/claim.yaml`, of the herdr pane where the _Assigned_Agent_ runs: the herdr session socket, the pane id, the agent kind and the agent session id.
.relations
  references _adoc:Adoc_Web_UI_
  references _adoc:Adoc_Workspace_
  references _adoc:User_Message_
  identifies _Assigned_Agent_
  written by _Agent_Claim_Command_
  read by _Adoc_Server_
  inside _Adoc_Home_
  targets _User_Message_Transport_
.contract
  - An _Adoc_Workspace_ must have at most one _Agent_Claim_; a new claim replaces the old one, and the old pane stops being the _Assigned_Agent_.
  - The _Adoc_Server_ must follow changes of `.adoc/claim.yaml` while it runs, and must show the claimed pane and its agent status in the _Adoc_Web_UI_.
  - When the claimed pane closes, the _Adoc_Server_ must keep the claim but show it as gone and hold every _User_Message_ until a new claim.
  - `.adoc/claim.yaml` must not be committed; `adoc init` must list it in `.adoc/.gitignore`.
.remarks
  - Chosen: a separate file rather than `.adoc/adoc.yaml`, because the claim belongs to one computer and changes often.
}

procedure _Agent_Claim_Command_ in surface = {
  The `adoc agent claim` command with which an agent makes its own herdr pane the _Assigned_Agent_ of the workspace; `adoc agent show` prints the current _Agent_Claim_.
.relations
  references _adoc:Adoc_Server_
  part of _Adoc_CLI_
  invoked by _Assigned_Agent_
  writes _Agent_Claim_
.contract
  - _Agent_Claim_Command_ must find the pane in this order: the pane given by `--pane`; else the pane whose recorded agent session equals the caller's session id (`CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`, `CODEX_SESSION_ID`), searched in every herdr session; else `HERDR_PANE_ID` with `HERDR_SOCKET_PATH`, unless the caller descends from a shared agent daemon such as `codex app-server`.
  - _Agent_Claim_Command_ must fail with a clear error naming `--pane` when none of these finds a pane.
  - `adoc server run --agent-pane <pane>` must write the same _Agent_Claim_ before the _Adoc_Server_ starts.
.remarks
  - Chosen: the order follows herdr-connect, whose tools may run in another process than the agent's pane.
  - Example: the agent runs `adoc agent claim` once at the start of a session; claiming again from another pane takes the role over.
}

concept _Agent_Terminal_Stream_ in runtime = {
  The live terminal of the pane named by the _Agent_Claim_, which the _Adoc_Server_ relays between herdr and the browser sessions.
.relations
  references _adoc:Adoc_Web_UI_
  relayed by _Adoc_Server_
  shows pane of _Agent_Claim_
  controlled by _Browser_Session_
.contract
  - The _Adoc_Server_ must take the stream from `herdr terminal session control` for the one _Browser_Session_ that controls the terminal, and from `herdr terminal session observe` for every other one.
  - The controlling _Browser_Session_ is the one the user used last: it takes control when it loads with focus and on any click, key press or focus in its page; it must send keys as `terminal.input`, its terminal size as `terminal.resize`, and wheel scrolling as `terminal.scroll` with a direction and a number of lines, so that the wheel scrolls the pane's scrollback rather than reaching the program as keys, and mouse buttons as `terminal.mouse` with an action, a button and a 0-based cell.
  - The _Adoc_Server_ must subscribe again when herdr drops the event subscription, for example after herdr restarts.
  - An observing _Browser_Session_ that receives no frame for three seconds must re-open its stream, because herdr's observe stream can lag behind agent panes.
  - The _Adoc_Server_ must send `terminal.release` when the controlling _Browser_Session_ closes or another one takes control, so that the user's own herdr terminal gets its size back.
  - The _Adoc_Server_ must subscribe to the agent status and the closing of the claimed pane through herdr events and pass them to the _Adoc_Web_UI_.
.remarks
  - Chosen: herdr's own session stream rather than a PTY attach or the herdr TUI, so that adoc needs no node-pty.
  - Chosen: the controlling browser resizes the pane to its own terminal size while it controls it.
  - Chosen: mouse events need herdr 0.9.3 or later; herdr passes them to the program only when the program tracks the mouse.
}
